  roleInSystem:"Delivers large assemblies straight to the line - bumpers and cockpit modules, door trims and seats, windscreens and windows, sheet-metal chassis frames and fuel tanks, and steel or alloy wheels. These are bulky parts made close to the vehicle plant, often in sequence with the assembly line.",
  whyItMatters:"These are the biggest-ticket parts by size and a large share of a vehicle's bill of materials. Suppliers that sit next to every big plant (Motherson globally, Asahi in glass) are hard to replace, while sheet-metal and wheel makers follow the volumes of a few anchor customers.",
  valuePoolDescription:"Motherson is the largest Indian auto-parts group by revenue, with most of it earned abroad (bumpers, mirrors, modules, wiring). Asahi India Glass makes most of the glass in Indian cars. Belrise (listed 28 May 2025) makes sheet-metal and chassis parts mainly for two-wheelers; Steel Strips Wheels and Wheels India make wheels for cars, trucks and tractors. Tata AutoComp (unlisted) supplies interiors and plastics to Tata and others.",
